 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-id1396394\" class=\"interactive\" data-label=\"\">\n<h2 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h2>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<h3 data-type=\"title\" class=\"os-subtitle\">\n  <span class=\"os-subtitle-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h3>\n<span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-id2050875\" data-alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20240910.161227/resources/90380e40da3ba36bdc3b79a302394bd6212e5435\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\">\n</span>\n<p id=\"fs-id1473369\">Watch what occurs at the G<sub>1</sub>, G<sub>2</sub>, and M checkpoints by visiting this <a href=\"https://openstaxcollege.org/l/cell_checkpnts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">website</a> to see an animation of the cell cycle.</p>\n</div>\n</div>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 639674,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Down Syndrome is a genetic, developmental condition caused by nondisjunction of chromosome 21 during meiosis. Explain how a problem with the spindle checkpoint can cause this to occur in the cell.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246233,
     "content_html": "Failure in spindle checkpoint results in the formation of one gamete cell with two extra chromosomes and another gamete cell lacking chromosomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246232,
     "content_html": "Failure in spindle checkpoint yields the same number of chromosomes in each gamete cell."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246231,
     "content_html": "Failure in spindle checkpoint will form two gamete cells without any chromosomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246234,
     "content_html": "Failure in spindle checkpoint results in the formation of one gamete cell with an extra chromosome and another gamete cell lacking a chromosome."
    }
   ],
